# data/RB_DERIV/ (the dataset) and data/baseline/ (the comparison point) MUST
# be tracked -- they make this project self-contained. data/artifacts/ holds
# the memory bank, traces and vectors copied from the RoT project (12M), plus
# the regenerable T3 rewrites; it travels by rsync, like the RoT project's.
data/artifacts/
# Raw per-problem rows are regenerable and large; the summary tables are the
# findings and are small, so they are tracked. A run's
# numbers should survive a laptop, and the GPU box is shared -- jobs there get
# killed to free VRAM.
#
# NOTE the `results/**` form. Writing `results/` here instead would exclude the
# DIRECTORY, and git never descends into an excluded directory -- every `!` line
# below would then be silently dead. The `!results/*/` line is required for the
# same reason: the run subdirectories have to be re-included before anything
# inside them can be.
results/**
!results/*/
!results/*/summary.md
!results/*/summary.csv
!results/*/summary.json
!results/*/by_group.csv
!results/*/run_manifest.json
!results/*/config.snapshot.yaml

logs/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
